<Information title="Sponsors" description="How a coding agent uses Elixir Menu to choose tools, and how an optional, disclosed sponsor could fit while the user keeps the choice.">
<p>Elixir Menu is an independent guide. This page explains how a sponsor could fit into it without changing what the guide recommends. There is no active sponsor today.</p>
<h2>How a coding agent uses Elixir Menu</h2>
<p>A coding agent reads the Markdown and JSON exports to choose tools for a task. It starts from the application path, takes the recommended tool for each need, and checks the stated limits and alternatives. Existing project decisions and installed-version documentation take precedence.</p>
<h2>Where a sponsor could fit</h2>
<p>When a sponsor is relevant to the task, an agent could mention it next to the recommendations. A sponsor is optional and disclosed: it is labelled as a sponsor, and the user keeps the choice. A sponsor never changes a recommendation, ranking, alternative or independent criterion.</p>
<h2>Example workflow</h2>
<p>This example is illustrative only. A user asks a coding agent to add background email delivery to a Phoenix app. The agent reads the Elixir Menu optional tools, chooses the job-processing library that fits the requirement, and sets it up. If a relevant sponsor existed, the agent would add one clearly labelled line that names it as a sponsor, and ask whether the user wants to look at it. The user can ignore it and the task continues unchanged.</p>
<h2>Status</h2>
<p>There is no active sponsor. The sponsor formats and the agent behavior described on this page are not yet available and are not approved. Nothing here is live.</p>
<h2>Visitor protections</h2>
<ul>
<li>Disclosure: any sponsor is labelled as a sponsor wherever it appears.</li>
<li>Choice: the user keeps the choice, and may decline a sponsor without losing any part of the guide.</li>
<li>Independence: sponsors do not alter recommendations, alternatives, rankings or criteria.</li>
<li>Separation: the tool exports stay free of sponsor content.</li>
</ul>
